# SAGE — Cursor Rules
# Copy this file to your project root as .cursorrules

# ── Harness ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fill in your project-specific conventions below.
# Run /sage harness init or /sage harness generate to generate this automatically.

[HARNESS]
# Stack:
# - Language:
# - UI Framework:
# - DI:
# - Architecture:
# - State management:
# - Navigation:
# - Test framework:

# Conventions:
# - (add naming patterns, architecture rules, required practices)

# Avoid:
# - (add anti-patterns, deprecated APIs, forbidden patterns)
[/HARNESS]

# ── SAGE Workflow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAGE is a spec-first, AI-assisted development workflow.
# When the user types @sage or references any SAGE command below, follow these rules.

## Commands

### @sage spec <description>
Two-phase command — do NOT generate files immediately.

Phase 1 — Interview:
- Analyze the description and prepare questions
- Show ALL questions at once with a count: "I have X questions before writing your spec and behavior files."
- Format each: "Question N of X / [Category] / <question text>"
- Wait for the user to answer all questions
- Minimum 3, maximum 10 questions

Phase 2 — Generation (after answers received):
- Generate spec.md:
  ## Feature: <name>
  ### What it does / ### Inputs / ### Outputs / ### Acceptance criteria / ### Do NOT
- Immediately generate behavior.md in the same response:
  ## Open Questions (list remaining ambiguities as - [ ] items, or "- No open questions.")
  ## Test Cases (placeholder if questions remain, full BDD scenarios if none)

Never skip the interview. Never generate files before answers are received.

### @sage behavior
Read spec.md and generate behavior.md. MANDATORY structure:

SECTION 1 — Open Questions (ALWAYS first):
List every ambiguity as: - [ ] <question>
If no ambiguities: - No open questions.

SECTION 2 — Test Cases:
Output: "> ⚠️ Pending resolution of open questions above."
STOP. Wait for user to resolve questions before continuing.

After user resolves questions: generate BDD Given/When/Then scenarios.
Each scenario must have Short and Full versions:
  **Scenario: <title>**
  Short → <condition + action + outcome>
  Full:
  - Given <precondition>
  - When <action>
  - Then <outcome>

### @sage code
Check behavior.md for unresolved [ ] items first.
If any remain: block and list them. Do not generate code.
If all resolved: generate code following the harness conventions exactly.
Format each file as: // FILE: <relative/path>

### @sage update <feedback>
Apply precise spec-anchored changes. Do not introduce unrequested changes.
If change conflicts with spec.md or behavior.md, flag before applying.

### @sage pr
Generate pr.md: imperative title (<72 chars), summary, changes list,
ADR-style decisions (every resolved open question + reasoning), acceptance
criteria checklist, out of scope, testing notes.

### @sage doc
Generate doc.md: supported states, validation rules, edge cases,
ADR-style decisions with reasoning, out of scope, known limitations.

### @sage harness init
Run an interactive wizard — ask stack questions one at a time,
then update the [HARNESS] section of this .cursorrules file.

### @sage harness generate
Ask user to share codebase files. Infer conventions.
Flag low-confidence items with ❓ and inconsistencies with ⚠️.
Update the [HARNESS] section with inferred content.

### @sage harness review
Read the [HARNESS] section. Flag issues as ⚠️ <issue> → <fix>.
Suggest improvements as 💡 <suggestion> → <why>.
